  "final_verdict": "NO EVIDENCE OF PREDICTIVE EDGE",
  "verdict_rationale": "Out-of-sample evaluation across 516 institutional gold sessions (2023\u20132024) reveals that daily macroeconomic changes (10-Year Real Yields, Broad Dollar Index, Breakeven Inflation) possess no statistically credible predictive power for next-session XAUUSD returns. Out-of-sample correlation with next-session returns is near zero (|r| <= 0.0244, p > 0.57), regression R-squared is zero (R2 <= 0.0006), and directional hit rates (49.7% to 51.4%) fail to beat a random coin toss. Net of realistic execution and financing costs ($0.42 to $0.66/oz), every active macro model loses money (-$79.02/oz to -$297.18/oz, Net PF 0.894 to 0.978) and is outperformed by the No-Trade baseline ($0.00). All candidate models fail the pre-registered promotion hurdle of Net PF > 1.25 and fail Holm-Bonferroni significance testing. The data firmly rejects the hypothesis that 1-day macro changes forecast next-session gold returns.",
